<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bawlake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">19th century–1948</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bawlake was one of the Karenni States in the hills of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, a small chiefdom ruled by a hereditary saopha. Like its neighbours <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kantarawaddy">Kantarawaddy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyebogyi">Kyebogyi</a>, it was recognised as independent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the Burmese king in 1875 and became a British feudatory in 1892. It joined the Union of Burma in 1948, and its territory now lies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayah-state">Kayah State</a>.</p></div>
